Subject: [PATCH] base: set the ICU default timezone from the device profile

InitializeICU runs unconditionally in every process type, which is what makes it
the right place. The browser, every renderer and every worker share one ICU
default, and a process that missed the override would disagree with the others
about what time it is — comparing a Date in a worker against one on the main
thread is a two-line probe.

Only the zone name comes from the profile. ICU's data is compiled into the
binary and file access is restricted to packages at startup, so the zone list,
the calendar list and every DST rule already come from our own build and are
identical on every host. That was measured rather than assumed: the data file
carries 447 canonical zones, the enumeration excludes 29 region-001 entries, and
418 is exactly the supportedTimeZonesCount our capture reports.

createTimeZone returns the "unknown" zone rather than null for a name ICU does
not carry, and adopting that would silently produce UTC — a wrong answer that
looks like a working one. Unknown names are rejected and the host zone kept.

Deliberately not patched: the Blink-side TimeZoneController, whose only other
production caller is the CDP emulation agent. Setting the ICU default reaches
every context through the same path Chromium already uses for a real timezone
change.

Ledger: intl.resolved-timezone, browser.icu-default, worker.date-timezone,
coh.timezone-across-contexts.

diff --git a/base/apostate/profile.cc b/base/apostate/profile.cc
index adce0ad..d2727ce 100644
--- a/base/apostate/profile.cc
+++ b/base/apostate/profile.cc
@@ -164,6 +164,12 @@ Profile* Profile::ParseOrNull(const std::string& encoded) {
     }
   }
 
+  if (const DictValue* locale = dict->FindDict("locale")) {
+    if (const std::string* v = locale->FindString("timezone")) {
+      profile->timezone_ = *v;
+    }
+  }
+
   if (const DictValue* browser = dict->FindDict("browser")) {
     if (const std::string* v = browser->FindString("user_agent")) {
       profile->user_agent_ = *v;
diff --git a/base/apostate/profile.h b/base/apostate/profile.h
index dc2b9e9..5f924bc 100644
--- a/base/apostate/profile.h
+++ b/base/apostate/profile.h
@@ -137,6 +137,14 @@ class BASE_EXPORT Profile {
   // depth, and the same fact drives CSS color, dynamic-range and color-gamut.
   std::optional<int> screen_color_depth() const { return screen_color_depth_; }
 
+  // IANA timezone name, e.g. "Europe/Warsaw".
+  //
+  // Only the zone *name* is a host fact. ICU's data is compiled into the binary
+  // and file access is restricted to packages at startup, so the zone list and
+  // every DST rule come from our own build and are identical on every host —
+  // free to get right, and impossible to get wrong per-host.
+  const std::optional<std::string>& timezone() const { return timezone_; }
+
   // Identifier of the capture this profile was derived from, for diagnostics.
   const std::string& source_id() const { return source_id_; }
 
@@ -161,6 +169,7 @@ class BASE_EXPORT Profile {
   std::optional<int> screen_avail_height_;
   std::optional<float> device_scale_factor_;
   std::optional<int> screen_color_depth_;
+  std::optional<std::string> timezone_;
   std::string source_id_;
 };
 
diff --git a/base/i18n/icu_util.cc b/base/i18n/icu_util.cc
index 0261246..b22b735 100644
--- a/base/i18n/icu_util.cc
+++ b/base/i18n/icu_util.cc
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
 
 #include "base/i18n/icu_util.h"
 
+#include "base/apostate/profile.h"
+
 #include "build/build_config.h"
 
 #if BUILDFLAG(IS_WIN)
@@ -399,7 +401,39 @@ bool InitializeICUWithFileDescriptor(
     return false;
   }
 
-  return DoCommonInitialization();
+  if (!DoCommonInitialization()) {
+    return false;
+  }
+
+  // Apostate: set the default zone here, immediately after ICU is initialised
+  // and in whatever process is initialising it.
+  //
+  // InitializeICU runs unconditionally in every process type, which is what
+  // makes this the right place: the browser, every renderer and every worker
+  // share one ICU default, and a process that missed the override would
+  // disagree with the others about what time it is. Comparing a Date in a
+  // worker against one on the main thread is a two-line probe.
+  //
+  // Only the zone name is taken from the profile. ICU's data is compiled into
+  // the binary and file access is restricted to packages at startup, so the
+  // zone list and every DST rule already come from our own build.
+  if (const ::base::apostate::Profile* profile =
+          ::base::apostate::Profile::Get()) {
+    if (profile->timezone().has_value()) {
+      std::unique_ptr<icu::TimeZone> zone(icu::TimeZone::createTimeZone(
+          icu::UnicodeString::fromUTF8(*profile->timezone())));
+      // createTimeZone returns the "unknown" zone rather than null for a name
+      // ICU does not carry; adopting that would silently produce UTC.
+      if (zone && *zone != icu::TimeZone::getUnknown()) {
+        icu::TimeZone::adoptDefault(zone.release());
+      } else {
+        LOG(ERROR) << "apostate: unknown timezone '" << *profile->timezone()
+                   << "'; keeping the host zone";
+      }
+    }
+  }
+
+  return true;
 }
 
